.TH UFLIB 7 "September 2026" "uflib 3.10.5" "UFSRV Programmer's Manual"
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH NAME
uflib \- foundational C library for the ufsrv messaging-server platform
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <uflib/utils.h>
.B #include <uflib/utils_crypto.h>
.B #include <uflib/adt/adt_hashtable.h>
.B #include <uflib/cdt/cdt_mpsc_queue.h>
.B #include <uflib/cdt/lockless_ringbuffer/cdt_lockless_ringbuffer.h>
.B #include <uflib/recycler_v2/recycler_v2.h>
.B #include <uflib/buffer_descriptor/buffer_descriptor.h>
.fi
.sp
Link with
.BR \-luflib .
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uflib
is the bottom layer of the ufsrv development stack.  It provides the
general-purpose software primitives every higher layer builds on: abstract
data types, lock-free concurrent data structures, an object recycler,
crypto and DB abstractions, networking helpers, coroutines, compression,
JSON, protobuf, UUID generation, and utility routines.  Dependencies flow
strictly downward \(em uflib has no visibility of ufsrvcorelib, ufnetcorelib,
or any application server.
.PP
uflib builds
.B libuflib_static.a
(and, when
.BR BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON ,
.BR libuflib.so )
from a single OBJECT library.  It is consumed by the higher layers via
.BR "find_package(uflib REQUIRED)" " + " uflib::uflib .
The library is written in C17 with GNU extensions, requires Clang, and is
licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or later.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH MODULES
.\" ===================================================
.SS Abstract data types \&(adt) \(em \fBadt/\fP
Classical single-threaded containers.
.PP
.TP
.B hashtable_v2
Open-addressing hash table.
.TP
.B hopscotch_hashtable_v2
Hopscotch hash table (bounded probe sequences).
.TP
.B distinct_array
Array of unique elements.
.TP
.B linkedlist / doubly_linkedlist
Intrusive singly- and doubly-linked lists.
.TP
.B queue
FIFO queue.
.TP
.B minheap
Single-threaded binary min-heap (priority queue).  Opaque handle; pointer-key
and inline-int64 key modes; any-magnitude comparator; geometric growth.
.BR MinHeapDescribe (MinHeap, bd)
emits state as JSON (size, capacity, mode, load factor, entries).
.TP
.B locking_lru
Mutex-protected least-recently-used cache.
.\" ===================================================
.SS Concurrent data types \&(cdt) \(em \fBcdt/\fP
Lock-free and lock-based structures for multi-threaded hot paths.  Each is
documented in its own design document under
.IR dev/technical_designs/ .
.PP
.TP
.B LamportQueue
Lock-free SPSC FIFO (two-index, one reserved slot).
.TP
.B LocklessMpscQueue
Intrusive lock-free MPSC (Vyukov).
.TP
.B LocklessFixedWidthHashMap
Lock-free fixed-width hash map (seq-lock + open addressing).
.TP
.B LocklessRingBuffer
Bounded copy-in/copy-out ring buffer with three concurrency modes \(em
SPSC, MPSC, and MPMC (Vyukov per-slot sequence numbers).
.TP
.B LocklessLRU
Lock-free approximate least-recently-used cache (CLOCK second-chance
eviction, per-slot seqlocks, upsert
.BR Set / SetEx ).
.TP
.B ChaseLevStealingQueue
Chase-Lev work-stealing deque.
.TP
.B AndersonSpinlock / MCSLock / spinlock
Lock-based synchronization primitives.
.TP
.B TreiberStack
Shared ABA-protected intrusive LIFO free-list (used by the recycler and
hash map).
.\" ===================================================
.SS Recycler \&(recycler, recycler_v2)
Object pooling with optional persistence.  A recycler allocates objects in
slab-like groups, hands them out through a lock-free free stack, and \(em in
V2 \(em can CLOCK-evict idle objects to disk and re-materialise them on
demand.
.PP
.TP
.B RecyclerV2InitTypePool(config)
Register a type pool.
.TP
.B RecyclerV2Get(handle, ctx, flags)
Lease an object (returns an
.BR InstanceHolderV2 ).
.TP
.B RecyclerV2Put(ih, ctx, flags)
Return an object to the pool.
.TP
.B RecyclerV2Referenced(ih, n) / RecyclerV2UnReferenced(ih, n)
External reference counting (multi-reference).
.TP
.B RecyclerV2GetNewInstance(ih) / RecyclerV2DestroyInstance(ih)
Multi-holder aliases for sharing one object.
.TP
.B RecyclerV2GetCapacity(handle) / RecyclerV2GetLeasedCount(handle)
Capacity and occupancy queries.
.TP
.B DescribeRecycler(type_pool_name, provided)
Describe pool state as a JSON string (all pools, or one by exact name).
.TP
.B ListRecyclerTypes()
List every registered type name in one contiguous allocation (free once).
.TP
.B RecyclerV2DumpState(stream) / RecyclerV2DumpStateToBuffer()
Full debug/introspection snapshot as JSON.
.\" ===================================================
.SS Buffer descriptor \&(buffer_descriptor)
A growable string builder used for console/JSON output.
.PP
.TP
.B BufferDescriptorInit(bd, cap)
Allocate the backing buffer (clamped to [64, 1 MiB]).
.TP
.B BufferDescriptorAppendFormatted(bd, fmt, ...)
Append printf-style output, growing as needed.
.TP
.B BufferDescriptorRelease(bd)
Free the backing buffer.
.\" ===================================================
.SS Utilities \&(utils*.h)
String, file, crypto, time, thread, and encoding helpers:
.BR utils_str ,
.BR utils_file ,
.BR utils_crypto ,
.BR utils_time ,
.BR utils_threads ,
.BR utils_base64 ,
.BR utils_base64url ,
.BR utils_hex ,
.BR utils_iec_quantity ,
.BR utils_urls ,
.BR utils_bits ,
.BR utils_sys ,
and
.BR tokeniser .
.\" ===================================================
.SS Persistence and networking \&(db, net)
.B db/
is a MariaDB/MySQL abstraction;
.B net/
provides networking helpers.  Both resolve OpenSSL through
.BR find_package(OpenSSL) .
.\" ===================================================
.SS Scheduled jobs \&(scheduled_jobs)
Scheduled task execution.
.\" ===================================================
.SS Embedded third-party libraries
.BR lzf " (compression), " mjson " (JSON), "
.BR protobuf-c ", " K12 " (KangarooTwelve), " uuid4 ", and " exponential_backoff
are vendored under
.IR src/ .
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH CONVENTIONS
Public functions are
.B PascalCase
with a module prefix, are annotated
.BR PUBLIC_API ,
and are declared in installed headers under
.IR include/uflib/ .
Opaque handles hide implementation layout; private headers under
.I src/
are never installed.  Lock-free CDTs additionally follow the design
correctness criteria in
.IR UF_LIBRARY_CONVENTIONS.md
(ABA, memory ordering, false sharing, reclamation, testing).
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
/* Lock-free SPSC ring buffer */
LocklessRingBuffer *ring =
    LocklessRingBufferCreate(1024, sizeof(int), LOCKLESS_RINGBUF_MODE_SPSC);

int in = 42, out;
while (!LocklessRingBufferTryPush(ring, &in)) { /* full: back off */ }
while (!LocklessRingBufferTryPop(ring, &out))  { /* empty: poll  */ }

LocklessRingBufferDestroy(ring);
.fi
.sp
See the runnable programs and gtest suites under
.IR tests/ .
